# carport, the numerical-carpet specification editor of ipl_gpacks (carpets), driven by its meta-key shortcuts: a definition added (sq as
# n * n), the modulus set to 7 and the neighborhood to n + w + sq through their dialogs, the definitions saved as t.defs (meta s; xencode of
# the table), meta q. Each dialog opens under the pointer and takes the keys there. LEFT OUT: generate (meta g, or Return in the main
# window) writes carpincl.icn and runs icont through system(); the specification's save (control meta w) fills its comments with &dateline.
# meta a: the add-definition dialog, its name field then its definition field
move 240 150
keydown Alt_L
key a
keyup Alt_L
wait
type sq
key Tab
type n * n
key Return
wait
# meta m: the modulus dialog, its field selected and typed over
keydown Alt_L
key m
keyup Alt_L
wait
type 7
key Return
wait
# meta n: the neighborhood dialog
keydown Alt_L
key n
keyup Alt_L
wait
type n + w + sq
key Return
wait
# meta s: the definitions saved through a file dialog
keydown Alt_L
key s
keyup Alt_L
wait
type t.defs
key Return
wait
# meta q quits (nothing in the database was changed, so it asks nothing)
keydown Alt_L
key q
keyup Alt_L
